    "content": "Here are the Austin‑specific grant opportunities that are currently listed:\n\n### Impact Austin Foundation Grants\n* **Who can apply:**  \n  * 501(c)(3) nonprofits and also non‑profit‑registered entities (or their fiscal sponsor) that register as a vendor with the City of Austin.  \n  * Applicants must serve the Austin‑Travis County area.  \n\n* **Key requirements:**  \n  * Only one submission per organization.  \n  * No insurance is required.  \n  * Awardees must:\n    * Participate in Equity Office‑sponsored trainings.  \n    * Host a site visit for Equity Office staff and join Equity Action Team meetings.  \n    * Deliver a final report (written or video) summarizing results, impact, challenges, and stories.  \n\n* **Application process:**  \n  * Review the **Impact Austin Grant Application Guidelines** and submit your proposal through the **Impact Austin Grants Management System**.  \n  * For questions, email **grants@impactaustin.org** or call **512‑553‑6083**.  \n\n* **Contact & administrative details:**  \n  * Impact Austin Foundation, P.O. Box 28148, Austin, TX 78755  \n  * Email: **contact@impactaustin.org**  \n  * The foundation is a Texas nonprofit exempt under IRS 501(c)(3) (EIN 56‑2367666).  \n\nThese details are taken directly from the Impact Austin Foundation’s grant information pages【1】 and the specific eligibility/requirements summary【2】. If you need the full application guidelines or the link to the Grants Management System, let me know and I can point you to the exact URLs.\n",
